:Panch Puran|Panch puran]] (futana / Bengali five spice)\n* 2 Indian [[Cookbook:Chiles|red chiles]] (sukhila lanka)\n* 10 [[Cookbook:Curry Leaf|curry leaves]] (kadi patta / bhersunga patra)\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Yogurt|dahi]] (yogurt)\n* 250 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] (1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]]) [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Cut eggplant into thin [[Cookbook:Slicing|slices]], lengthwise. [[Cookbook:Deep Fat Frying|Deep fry]] in oil. Keep aside. \n# Mix dahi with water.\n# Heat 1 tbsp of oil in a pan. Add panch puran and red chili, then cook until the spices splutter.\n# Add dahi-water mix, salt to taste, and sugar. Stir properly and make a gravy.\n# Add fried eggplant to the gravy, and lower the flame.\n# Heat it for 2–3 minutes, then leave it to cool.\n# Serve with rice.\n\n[[Category:Indian recipes]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Naturally gluten-free recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using curry leaf]]\n[[Category:Recipes using yogurt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using eggplant]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Dahi Baingana (Fried Eggplant in Yogurt)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 medium-sized bainganas (eggplant / brinjal / begun)","sourceText":"2 medium-sized bainganas (eggplant / brinjal / begun)","amountText":"2 medium-sized bainganas (eggplant / brinjal / begun)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"Oil","sourceText":"Oil","amountText":"Oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"Panch puran (futana / Bengali five spice)","sourceText":"Panch puran (futana / Bengali five spice)","amountText":"Panch puran (futana / Bengali five spice)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"